text.text:
I came here for lunch. We did not get the whole tasting menu, but we did try a lot of different items so we tried the lobster, hiramasa, tuna and fluke. obviously everything was delicious and well presented, the staff was super helpful. We were asking questions and they were more than happy to oblige. They made recommendations on the drinks and they also helped us to decide which dishes we should order so that they complemented each other since we were sharing.

It’s definitely white tablecloth kind of seating and the tone of the restaurant seemed relatively laid-back. I saw people in general business tire I saw one lady wearing shorts and some men were without jackets so I did not think it was incredibly formal which is nice for summer afternoon. They also allow very well behaved dogs because we saw a really sweet poodle in there. perhaps it gets more up scale at dinner time.

for dessert, I tried the peach cottage cheese dish, and the person I was with tried the macaroons, both really good but I think I preferred mine thankfully. I would definitely recommend a visit at least once :)

